# The Godot runtime CI uses, pinned, with the digest that makes the pin mean
# something. One version, never "latest": a digest only says anything about a file
# that cannot change, and `latest` changes under it.
#
# THIS IS THE SECOND COPY OF THIS PIN AND THE DRIFT IS GUARDED.
#
# The first is dot-server-deploy/tools/fetch-godot.sh, which is authoritative: it is
# the pin the containers, the release tarballs and every developer box are built from,
# and it carries the digests for three platforms because those have to run everywhere.
# CI only ever needs Linux x86_64, and reaching into a private repository to read one
# string before it can fetch anything would put that repository in front of every
# check in the family.
#
# So it is copied, and dot-server-deploy's own workflow compares the two and fails
# when they disagree -- the drift is caused THERE and would be suffered HERE, so the
# check belongs on the side that can name the person who moved the pin. Moving it
# means editing both, in the same change.
#
# To move it: take the digest from that release's own SHA512-SUMS.txt, with your own
# eyes, and paste it. Never from beside the binary -- a checksum served by whoever
# served the zip is checked by whoever would have had to tamper with both.
#
#   curl -fsSL https://github.com/godotengine/godot/releases/download/4.7.2-stable/SHA512-SUMS.txt

GODOT_VERSION=4.7.2-stable
SHA512_linux_x86_64=9aa00f7a605200940bce3027a567b782f49bd8e940dd06ae9e987bd65aee1b1467edd56ed84fcdcbdd44354bf613bdbb4e5d2913e925850368e150c59ed54c65
